    "family": {
        "id": "polynomial-multiplication-baselines",
        "issue": "c7113c5a",
        "purpose": "kernel-family",
        "description": "Current-code gf2 baselines against pinned gf2x 1.3.0 for the three gf2 operations that have an equivalent gf2x form: the unreduced long product in GF(2)[x], the batch of independent unreduced 64-by-64 products, and the whole-consumer GF(2^8) dot product whose unreduced stage is composed from gf2x products and reduced by gf2's own Barrett reducer on both arms. Sizes span the small fixed-width field operands, the crossover region of gf2x's Karatsuba and Toom thresholds, a cache-resident size and a streaming size, with single-core latency and six-, twelve- and twenty-four-way throughput arms. Every cell is a comparator gap: this survey adopts nothing, adds no gf2x production dependency and changes no gf2 multiplication algorithm, so a measured gap is an attribution task rather than a selection. This addendum supersedes addendum-polynomial-baselines.json. It carries that addendum's ten cells unchanged, so the campaign it governs re-measures them, and adds a six-cell build ladder that closes REQ-05: two operand sizes, one where gf2's dispatched kernel leads and one where gf2x's subquadratic path leads, each measured under the conservative, tuned and native build of both sides. The gf2 side's build identity is the cell's builds.baseline; the gf2x side is builds.candidate 'external' in every cell because the schema has one external identity, so the launcher pairs each cell with the gf2x arm of the matching variant (gf2-conservative with gf2x-conservative, gf2-tuned with gf2x-tuned, gf2-native with gf2x-native) and the receipt's arm descriptors record which library each arm mapped. The native legs duplicate the operand sizes of poly-mul-4w-1core and poly-mul-256w-1core on purpose: the three legs of each ladder then differ only in build identity, and the duplicate is a same-campaign replicate of an existing cell. The ten carried cells are re-measured rather than cited from the version-1 receipt for two reasons: that receipt records six of them as unstable under the version-1 pooled flagged-window rule, and one campaign gives the ladder and the ten cells one host, one session ledger and one Bonferroni correction. Re-measuring them is a second confirmatory attempt on the same candidate identity, which max_confirmatory_attempts_per_candidate of 1 permits only under a new protocol version, so this addendum is held until protocol version 2 lands and is re-stamped with that version and a fresh frozen_utc before it runs; the first attempt is declared in family_wise.prior_trials and counts in the family either way."
    },
    "frozen": {
        "frozen_utc": "2026-09-08T13:05:00Z"
    },
    "effect": {
        "worthwhile_speedup": null,
        "rationale": "This family declares no improvement cell. Every cell compares gf2 against an external library under a material-gap threshold, and the issue excludes adoption, so no worthwhile-speedup threshold applies and none is invented.",
        "measurement_resolution": 0.08,
        "resolution_evidence": {
            "receipt": "dev/bench_results/c7113c5a/2026-09-07-c7113c5a-polynomial-pilot/receipt.json",
            "sha256": "22d2663f89f32bc0cccbd6baebad6c1b054ac04f408311a97b79790af7ecaed1"
        },
        "equivalence_margin": 1.15,
        "equivalence_rationale": "A fifteen-percent band sits above the 0.08 resolution the pilot measured, so a not-worse verdict is a statement the host can support rather than an artefact of the interval width. It is also the scale below which a consumer choosing between the two libraries would decide on portability and licensing rather than on speed, given that gf2x is GPL-3.0-or-later and gf2 is MIT.",
        "material_gap_threshold": 1.25,
        "material_gap_rationale": "A quarter of the runtime is the smallest gap that survives the adapter and conversion costs a real consumer pays to reach an external library, so it is the smallest gap that would change an engineering decision. It is more than three times the 0.08 resolution the pilot measured, so a material-gap verdict is not a resolution artefact."
    },
